Build 027: the frame capture names the programs that last wrote each image (writers.txt next to
index.txt). The 026 capture showed the overexposure in one 1920x1080 B10G11R11 target written after the
correctly lit scene (R and G up to 65,000, B about 1), and an empty nearest shadow cascade; this tells
which pipeline writes them. The rasterizer sets a per-thread writer around draws (vertex-slot and pixel
program addresses), clears (rt0) and compute dispatches (program address); MarkModification copies it
into the image. Diagnostic only: nothing drawn changes.

diff --git a/src/video_core/native_draw_trace.h b/src/video_core/native_draw_trace.h
--- a/src/video_core/native_draw_trace.h
+++ b/src/video_core/native_draw_trace.h
@@ -83,6 +83,28 @@
     return it->second;
 }
 
+/// What writes images on this thread right now, for the frame capture's writers.txt (which program
+/// drew the overexposed target): the rasterizer sets it around a draw (kind 1: the vertex-slot and
+/// pixel programs' addresses), a clear (2: the first colour target) and a compute dispatch (3: the
+/// program's address); anything else (copies, blits, uploads) leaves kind 0. The addresses match
+/// the "Lowered native shader at ..." lines, which give their keys.
+struct Writer {
+    u32 kind{};
+    u64 first{};
+    u64 second{};
+};
+inline thread_local Writer current_writer{};
+struct WriterScope {
+    explicit WriterScope(Writer writer) {
+        current_writer = writer;
+    }
+    ~WriterScope() {
+        current_writer = {};
+    }
+    WriterScope(const WriterScope&) = delete;
+    WriterScope& operator=(const WriterScope&) = delete;
+};
+
 /// Frames counted by RasterizerVulkan::TickFrame.
 inline std::atomic<u64> frame{};
 
